connection-rule-448f52d5.conceptual_definition:
The relation $\Gamma^\lambda_{\mu
u} = \Gamma^\lambda_{
u\mu}$ is the mathematical statement that the connection is symmetric. This is equivalent to the vanishing of the torsion tensor, defined as $T^\lambda_{\mu
u} = \Gamma^\lambda_{\mu
u} - \Gamma^\lambda_{
u\mu}$. A torsion-free, or symmetric, connection implies that infinitesimal parallelograms formed by parallel transport along two vector fields will close. In the context of Riemannian geometry, the unique connection that is both metric-compatible and torsion-free is the Levi-Civita connection.
